A||||13||fierogt88||considering swapping a 4.3||||1||
Z||000000||fierogt88||04-12-2001||10:17 AM||||I knew that my fiero would be getting an engine swap even before I started to shop for the car.  After spending the last eight months here, I've come to the conclusion that I want something a little different.  I have seen a picture of a 4.3 in a fiero, and I think this is the swap for me.  I need to do a lot of research before taking the plunge, so anybody who can point me to any good resources, please do so.<P><BR>The main point of this post is to get some preliminary info.  Can the V8 conversion kits that are out there be used for the 4.3?  Do they use the same motor mounts?  I've heard that the archie kit moves the transmission 1/2 inch.  Will this be necessary (or avoidable) for a 4.3 swap?  Will I have to notch the frame?  Archie, do you have any experience with 4.3 swaps?<P>I found out that superchargers for the 4.3 are available, but that they are sold for the 96 to 98 blazers/s10's, so i'm assuming that this is for a fuel injection setup, but is there something special about the 96 to 98 s10's/blazers since these are the only compatible years?  Is this what I should be pricing at the boneyards?<P>Since the 4.3 is so similar to the 350, a lot of performance parts should be shareable between the two, but what about things like crank and cams?  any performance pieces like that available?<P>What about electronics?  Do I want to get it out of a 2 wheel drive instead of a 4 wheel drive or does the s10 computer even care?  I guess I'm wondering if I'm going to see any problems like the northstar guys where you get stuck in limp mode for not providing the computer with enough info.<P>Well, that's a lot of questions!  Before anyone jumps on here and tells me not to bother and to just go to 3.4/3.8/350  I would say don't waste your time, because the "unusualness" of the 4.3 is what I'm shooting for, and it should seriously stomp other "unusual" swaps like the quad4.||||reg||1
Z||000001||BigTurbo87GT||04-12-2001||11:03 AM||||I can provide some very educated guesses to spur somebody who knows to chime in.<P>The bell housing pattern for a 4.3 is the same as for a V8 (sbc anyway).<P>The newer engines added balance shafts, this apparently was a significant change.<P>There are two version of the 4.3, a 175ish hp one and a 190hp one. My guess is that you would want the 190 one.<P>If you really wanna go nuts, check out gm performance parts, they have aluminum blocks and just about everything else you need to make a screamer.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierojunky||04-12-2001||11:19 AM||||The base S-10/blazers have the 175/180HP 4.3 - the extreemes and the ZR-2's have the HO 4.3 190HP - The extreeme has only been out for 2 years so i would try to find one out of a ZR-2 or as GMC calls them the Highrider.  The 4.3 in my Z is very powerfull i have considered swapping it in my car and putting an LT-1 in the truck - happy hunting and keep us updated on the progress.||||reg||14
