Z||000004||fierogt88||04-12-2001||11:33 AM||||I have heard from a very reliable source that the extra journals and lobes can be used to power a flux capacitor, netting about 35 extra butterflypower.  The extra radiation, however, would require that the entire engine be filled with lead implanted silicone, so maybe it would be in my best interests to just find stuff for a six cylinder.  Or maybe the flux capacitor is the way to go.... any suggestions?<P>// Edit:  hmmm. TerryK, I took that in good humor.  I could see where my cam question was a little confusing.  You didn't have to get rid of it    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierogt88 (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
